# Linux 7.2.12 display stack for the lmi (Xiaomi POCO F2 Pro) experiment.
#
# Scope: this fragment adds ONLY the display path that the observer kernel
# config never carried. Everything else stays exactly as validated by
# configs/observer-tested.config, which is the config that produced the
# accepted observer boot (kernel entry, eight CPUs, observer /init, HS USB
# RNDIS, journal retrieval).
#
# Why this fragment exists: the accepted observer config has no CONFIG_DRM at
# all, so the kernel has no KMS/DRM device, no DSI host, no MSM display
# controller and no panel driver. The white screen is the expected result of
# that configuration, not a panel or rail fault.
#
# Dependencies checked against upstream v7.2.12 sources:
#   CONFIG_DRM_MSM depends on DRM, ARCH_QCOM, COMMON_CLK, IOMMU_SUPPORT, OF,
#   PM and selects IOMMU_IO_PGTABLE, REGULATOR, DRM_EXEC, DRM_GPUVM,
#   DRM_SCHED, SHMEM, TMPFS, QCOM_SCM, QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG, PM_OPP, NVMEM,
#   PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS, TRACE_GPU_MEM and QCOM_MDT_LOADER.
#   The observer config already carries QCOM_SCM, IOMMU_SUPPORT,
#   IOMMU_IO_PGTABLE, COMMON_CLK, OF, PM_OPP, NVMEM and
#   REGULATOR_QCOM_RPMH, so no extra dependency has to be added here.
#
# DSI PHY: SM8250 is a 7 nm part, so CONFIG_DRM_MSM_DSI_7NM_PHY is the
# matching PHY (drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c), which is what
# upstream sm8250.dtsi binds through "qcom,dsi-phy-7nm".
#
# GPU: the same config brings up the Adreno 650 ("qcom,adreno-650.2" in
# upstream sm8250.dtsi). Upstream requests "qcom/a650_sqe.fw",
# "qcom/a650_gmu.bin" and "qcom/a650_zap.mdt" (a6xx_catalog.c); the matching
# files are already in the project at userspace/gpu/files/firmware/a650/ and
# must be placed under /lib/firmware/qcom/ in the initramfs. If they are
# missing, the GPU probe fails and no DRM device is created, so the panel
# stays dark even if the DSI wiring is correct.
#
# BUILT-IN, NOT MODULE: the observer initramfs carries no module payload, so
# every symbol on the display path has to be compiled in. This is not
# cosmetic: with CONFIG_DRM_MSM=m the kernel never creates a DRM device, the
# panel stays dark, and the journal shows no msm_drm probe at all.
#
# WHY CONFIG_MODULES=n IS PART OF THIS FRAGMENT
#
# The display chain cannot be forced to "y" while modules are enabled.
# CONFIG_DRM_MSM selects DRM_EXEC, DRM_GPUVM, DRM_SCHED, QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG
# and QCOM_MDT_LOADER. Those five are invisible tristate symbols, so the
# user cannot set them: with CONFIG_MODULES=y they take the value "m", and
# Kconfig caps a "y" symbol that selects a "m" symbol at "m" as well. The
# whole display stack therefore silently falls back to modules and never
# loads, which reproduces exactly the white screen of the observer kernel
# with nothing in the journal to explain it.
#
# Measured on this configuration: with CONFIG_MODULES=y every symbol of the
# chain ends up "m" (five independent experiments), and with CONFIG_MODULES=n
# they all end up "y". Disabling modules removes exactly one symbol from
# this configuration, CONFIG_CRYPTO_BENCHMARK, which is a crypto self-test
# module and is irrelevant to this handset. All other 925 modular symbols of
# the observer configuration belong to other platforms and could never load
# from an initramfs without a module payload anyway.
#
# Kconfig symbols added by the panel patch:
#   CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_SAMSUNG_AMS667UU01

CONFIG_MODULES=n

CONFIG_DRM=y
CONFIG_DRM_EXEC=y
CONFIG_DRM_GPUVM=y
CONFIG_DRM_SCHED=y
CONFIG_DRM_KMS_HELPER=y
CONFIG_DRM_MSM=y
CONFIG_DRM_MSM_KMS=y
CONFIG_DRM_MSM_DSI=y
CONFIG_DRM_MSM_DSI_7NM_PHY=y
CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_SAMSUNG_AMS667UU01=y
CONFIG_QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG=y
CONFIG_QCOM_MDT_LOADER=y

# Panel driver prerequisites.
CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE=y
CONFIG_REGULATOR=y
CONFIG_GPIOLIB=y
